)F FUNCTION -                                                           02000020
  THE LOGON COMMAND INITIATES A TERMINAL JOB.                           04000020
)X SYNTAX -                                                             06000020
         LOGON   'ID' ACCT('ACCOUNT') PROC('PROCEDURE') SIZE('INTEGER') 08000020
                 PERFORM('INTEGER') GROUP('GROUP-ID') OIDCARD           10000003
                 MAIL/NOMAIL NOTICES/NONOTICES                          10010003
           OR                                                           10050002
         LOGON   'ID'  RECONNECT                                        10100002
  REQUIRED - 'ID'                                                       12000020
  DEFAULTS - ACCOUNT - NULL STRING                                      14000020
             PERFORM - SUPPLIED BY OPTIMIZER                            14050002
             GROUP   - DEFAULT FROM RACF PROFILE                        16000003
             MAIL                                                       16050003
             NOTICES                                                    16100003
        - WHEN USING TERMINALS SUPPORTED BY TSO/VTAM,                   16150003
          THE LOGON FROM THESE DEVICES WILL BE INSTALLATION DEFINED.    16200003
          SEE YOUR SYSTEM PROGRAMMER FOR YOUR INSTALLATIONS             16250003
          REQUIREMENTS.                                                 16300003
)O OPERANDS -                                                           16350003
  'ID'     - IS A USER'S IDENTIFICATION TO THE SYSTEM. THE 'ID'         16400003
             CONSISTS OF 'USERID/CURRENT-PASSWORD/NEW-PASSWORD'.        16450003
             IF THE USER DOES NOT HAVE PASSWORDS THEN                   16500003
             '/CURRENT-PASSWORD' IS OPTIONAL AND '/NEW-PASSWORD' IS     16550003
             IGNORED. '/NEW-PASSWORD' IS VALID ONLY FOR RACF USERS. IT  16600003
             WILL BECOME THE '/CURRENT-PASSWORD' THE NEXT TIME THE      16650003
             USER LOGS ON. IT WILL BE IGNORED FOR NON RACF USERS.       16700003
))ACCT('ACCOUNT')                                                       24000020
           - 'ACCOUNT' IS THE INFORMATION REQUIRED BY THE INSTALLATION  26000020
             ACCOUNTING ROUTINES.                                       28000020
))PROC('PROCEDURE')                                                     30000020
           - 'PROCEDURE' IS THE NAME OF A CATALOGUED PROCEDURE WHICH    32000020
             IDENTIFIES THE SYSTEM RESOURCES REQUIRED FOR A TERMINAL    34000020
             JOB.                                                       36000020
))SIZE('INTEGER')                                                       38000020
           - 'INTEGER' IS THE UPPER BOUND ON THE SIZE OF A VARIABLE     40000002
             CONDITIONAL GETMAIN WHICH CAN BE SATISFIED.                42000002
))PERFORM('INTEGER')                                                    42050002
           - 'INTEGER' IS A NUMBER FROM 1 TO 255, INCLUSIVE,            42100002
             INDICATING A PERFORMANCE GROUP FOR THIS SESSION.           42150002
))GROUP('GROUP-ID')                                                     42200003
           - 'GROUP-ID' IS VALID ONLY FOR RACF DEFINED USERS.           42250003
             IT IS A 1 TO 8 CHARACTER ID COMPOSED OF ALPHANUMERIC       42300003
             AND/OR NATIONAL CHARACTERS, THE FIRST OF WHICH MUST BE     42350003
             ALPHABETIC OR NATIONAL. IT WILL BE IGNORED FOR NON RACF    42400003
             USERS.                                                     42450003
))OIDCARD  - 'OIDCARD' IS VALID ONLY FOR RACF DEFINED USERS.            42500003
             SPECIFYING 'OIDCARD' ON LOGON WILL CAUSE THE USER          42550003
             TO BE PROMPTED FOR AN OPERATOR IDENTIFICATION CARD,        42600003
             EVEN IF AN OIDCARD IS NOT REQUIRED.  THE OPERATOR          42650003
             IDENTIFICATION CARD WILL ONLY BE ACCEPTED AFTER THE        42700003
             USER HAS BEEN PROMPTED TO ENTER ONE.  IT WILL BE           42750003
             IGNORED FOR NON RACF USERS.                                42800003
))MAIL     - SPECIFIES THAT ALL MESSAGES QUEUED ON THE BROADCAST DATA   44000020
             SET FOR THE USER ARE TO BE TRANSMITTED TO THE TERMINAL     46000020
             DURING LOGON PROCESSING AND THEN DELETED FROM THE DATA SET 48000020
))NOMAIL   - SPECIFIES THAT THE MESSAGES QUEUED ON THE BROADCAST DATA   50000020
             SET FOR THE USER ARE TO REMAIN QUEUED THERE FOR LATER      52000020
             TRANSMISSION.                                              54000020
))NOTICES  - SPECIFIES THAT THE MESSAGES QUEUED ON THE BROADCAST DATA   56000020
             SET WHICH ARE OF INTEREST TO ALL USERS SHOULD BE           58000020
             TRANSMITTED TO THE TERMINAL DURING LOGON PROCESSING.       60000020
))NONOTICES                                                             62000020
           - SPECIFIES THAT THE MESSAGES QUEUED ON THE BROADCAST DATA   64000020
             SET WHICH ARE OF INTEREST TO ALL USERS SHOULD NOT BE       66000020
             TRANSMITTED TO THE TERMINAL DURING LOGON PROCESSING.       68000020
))RECONNECT                                                             68050002
          - IF A USER'S LINE HAS BEEN DISCONNECTED HE MAY RELOGON USING 68100002
            THIS OPERAND - WHICH IS MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE OF ALL OTHERS.   68150002
            THE PASSWORD, IF ANY, USED WITH THE DISCONNECTED SESSION    68160002
            MUST BE USED WITH LOGON  'ID'  RECONNECT.                   68200002
